1. Different HTTP Methods. Difference Between POST and PUT.

1. GET – Retrieve data. POST – Create a resource or trigger processing. PUT – Create or completely replace a resource at a known URI. PATCH – Partially update a resource. DELETE – Delete a resource.
2. POST is generally not idempotent, meaning repeated requests may create multiple resources.
3. PUT is idempotent, meaning sending the same request multiple times should result in the same final state.
4. Example: POST /employees creates an employee, whereas PUT /employees/101 updates or replaces employee 101.

