14. How Can We Optimize UI Performance? What Does React Bring to the Table? Can We Optimize Without React?

1. Use lazy loading, pagination, caching, code splitting, image optimization, and debouncing to reduce unnecessary work.
2. React provides component-based architecture, reusable UI, state management patterns, and efficient DOM updates through reconciliation.
3. We can also optimize without React using JavaScript, browser DOM APIs, Web Components, and frameworks such as Angular or Vue.
4. React makes large interactive applications easier to maintain, but performance depends on component design, rendering, network calls, and data handling.

